The actual safe_math_macros_notmp.h helper narrows its subtraction result
to uint16_t. The finite tests exercise wrap boundaries and the first path's
16, 9, 2, 65531, 65524 progression; the range argument covers all u16 values.
This identifies repeating reached paths, not whole-program definedness or
a terminating checksum. Both original oracle-unusable outcomes remain.
